{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For</b> — Yet the wise die like everyone in every generation. He mentioned death together with the wise: they perish along with the fool and the brutish, for they go to Abaddon. The fool walks a crooked path, and the brutish does not understand, like the beast — and both perish." "<b>Their wealth</b> — corresponding to those who trust in their wealth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:15.635279273Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}